# {{ project_name }}

> {{ description }}

A full-stack Databricks solution whose job is to **create and update Terraform
agentically**. It runs as a Databricks Asset Bundle (DAB), authenticates as the
calling user{% if enable_obo %} (on-behalf-of){% endif %} for interactive runs and as a
{{ headless_auth | replace('_', ' ') }} for headless/scheduled runs, drafts or
edits Terraform under `{{ tf_dir }}/`, {% if run_terraform_plan %}runs `terraform plan`, {% endif %}and
opens a pull request against the
{% if git_host == "github" %}GitHub repo `{{ github_owner }}/{{ github_repo }}`{% else %}Azure DevOps repo `{{ ado_org }}/{{ ado_project }}/{{ ado_repo }}`{% endif %}.

It **never applies** Terraform directly — every change is proposed as a reviewable
pull request.

## Layout

```
{{ project_name }}/
├── AGENTS.md                       # Read this first (vendor-neutral agent doc).
├── CLAUDE.md                       # Pointer to AGENTS.md for Claude Code.
├── dex.toml                        # Project config: skills, passthroughs, tasks.
├── databricks.yml                  # DAB root.
├── resources/                      # DAB job{% if deploy_serving %} + serving endpoint{% endif %} definitions.
├── terraform/                      # Seed Terraform the agent maintains.
├── forms/
│   └── change_request.schema.json  # Dynamic form: attributes a change needs.
├── src/{{ project_name }}/
│   ├── agent.py                    # Entry point: plan -> draft -> validate -> PR.
│   ├── config.py                   # Settings from env + Databricks secrets.
│   ├── auth.py                     # OBO user / managed-identity resolution.
│   ├── git_host.py                 # Branch + PR client ({{ git_host }}).
│   ├── terraform.py                # fmt / validate / plan wrappers.
│   ├── llm.py                      # Model call that drafts Terraform.
│   ├── forms.py                    # Builds & auto-populates the change form.
│   ├── prompts/                    # system / generate / review prompts.
│   └── tools/                      # change_request, plan_reader (ToolResult).
├── evals/                          # Eval harness + cases (incl. a guardrail).
└── tests/                          # pytest unit tests.
```

## Quickstart

```bash
uv sync
uv run pytest

# Dry run — drafts the change locally, prints the diff and plan, opens no PR:
uv run python -m {{ project_name }}.agent --dry-run \
  "add a unity catalog schema named analytics with owner data_eng"
```

## Auth

| Mode | Used when | Identity |
|---|---|---|
| Interactive | a user invokes the agent | {% if enable_obo %}OBO — the calling user's token{% else %}user PAT{% endif %} |
| Headless | scheduled / job run | {{ headless_auth | replace('_', ' ') }} |

The git token used to push branches and open PRs is resolved in this order:
environment variable → Databricks secret scope `{{ secret_scope }}` → OBO token.
See `src/{{ project_name }}/auth.py`.

## Deploy

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
databricks bundle run {{ project_name }} --target dev
```
